WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.076 --> 00:00:01.485
Welcome to Bluff House

2
00:00:01.485 --> 00:00:04.494
where multiplayer blackjack meets social bluffing

3
00:00:04.494 --> 00:00:06.722
Step into an illustrated casino

4
00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:08.340
bring your friends to the table

5
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.673
and discover how quickly

6
00:00:09.673 --> 00:00:11.920
one bold decision can change the game

7
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.466
Create a private room and share its code

8
00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:16.472
Players join the same live lobby

9
00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.939
choose their avatars and ready up

10
00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:21.497
The host can customize the number of rounds

11
00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:24.920
starting chips timers and party features

12
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.517
The match begins with a secret auction for the house

13
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.631
Everyone can see who has submitted a bid

14
00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:31.980
while the amounts stay hidden until the reveal

15
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.598
Drew wins and becomes the player controlled dealer

16
00:00:34.598 --> 00:00:36.393
This role brings real stakes

17
00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:38.373
Personal chips are committed

18
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.655
dealer losses carry consequences

19
00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:42.870
and profitable rounds offer rewards

20
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.143
Build a custom wager

21
00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.513
by combining different chip denominations

22
00:00:46.597 --> 00:00:48.951
or use shortcuts like half and all in

23
00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:50.262
Once the cards arrive

24
00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:53.103
every player's hand and actions stay synchronized

25
00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:54.700
Then comes call my bluff

26
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.784
Blair claims the next hit won't bust

27
00:00:56.784 --> 00:00:58.415
Alex accepts the challenge

28
00:00:58.431 --> 00:00:59.860
putting chips on the line

29
00:00:59.877 --> 00:01:02.836
The server draws a 7 Blair busts at 27

30
00:01:02.836 --> 00:01:04.920
and Alex wins the funded challenge pot

31
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.048
Between rounds the competition goes beyond blackjack

32
00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:10.696
Split or steal asks whether you trust your opponent

33
00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:12.528
Here Blair chooses to split

34
00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.344
but Alex steals the entire pot

35
00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:17.100
Chaos cards introduce new tactical opportunities

36
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.516
including a boosted wager

37
00:01:18.516 --> 00:01:21.179
Players can also challenge each other to side games

38
00:01:21.225 --> 00:01:23.550
This connect four duel ends with four in a row

39
00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:24.905
and another pot awarded

40
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.366
The finale changes what everyone can see

41
00:01:27.366 --> 00:01:29.971
In Shadow Blackjack you know your own cards

42
00:01:29.971 --> 00:01:31.806
but opponents see only the first

43
00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:34.120
Alex's actual total is 13

44
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.109
yet the declaration is 21

45
00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:38.474
Other players have eight seconds to challenge

46
00:01:38.474 --> 00:01:41.834
Nobody calls so the bluff stands. At the showdown,

47
00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.731
that accepted 21 wins the remaining funded vault

48
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.727
The final standings bring together the matches wagers

49
00:01:47.727 --> 00:01:51.046
challenges and rivalries Alex finishes on top

50
00:01:51.046 --> 00:01:51.309
while

51
00:01:51.309 --> 00:01:54.184
illustrated achievement badges recognize the steals

52
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.404
victories and successful bluff that shaped this table

53
00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.920
Bluff House play bolder together
